IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-11.l4 -- ARTICLE 11: PROCESSING WHICH DOES NOT REQUIRE IDENTIFICATION.  Layer 1 (P1).
-- Whose duty and right: 11(1) frees the controller from an obligation (a no-duty: the controller's privilege and
-- the data subject's no-right); 11(2) first sentence is the controller's duty to inform the data subject (the
-- data subject's claim); 11(2) second sentence takes Articles 15 to 20 away from the data subject unless the data
-- subject gives identifying information (the data subject's power to restore them).  Articles 15 to 20 are P2's:
-- P2 takes `Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` as an input (PLAN.md section 4).
-- ============================================================================

DECLARE `Art 11(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `Art 11(2) inform the data subject accordingly`

§ `Article 11(1)`

-- src:140 | 1. If the purposes for which a controller processes personal data do not or do no longer require the identification of a data subject by the controller, the controller shall not be obliged to maintain, acquire or process additional information in order to identify the data subject for the sole purpose of complying with this Regulation.
@ref Art 11(1) (src:140)
GIVEN `the purposes for which the controller processes personal data do not or do no longer require the identification of a data subject by the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional information would be maintained, acquired or processed for the sole purpose of complying with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(1) the controller is obliged to maintain, acquire or process additional information in order to identify the data subject` MEANS
    IF `the purposes for which the controller processes personal data do not or do no longer require the identification of a data subject by the controller`
       AND `the additional information would be maintained, acquired or processed for the sole purpose of complying with this Regulation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, a flat negative): "If the purposes for which a controller processes personal data do not or do no longer require the identification of a data subject by the controller, the controller shall not be obliged to maintain, acquire or process additional information in order to identify the data subject for the sole purpose of complying with this Regulation."
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the freedom from the obligation is for the sole purpose of complying with this Regulation and where the purposes do not require identification; for any other case the text does not say

§ `Article 11(2), first sentence: inform the data subject`

-- src:141 | 2. Where, in cases referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject, the controller shall inform the data subject accordingly, if possible. In such cases, Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject, for the purpose of exercising his or her rights under those articles, provides additional information enabling his or her identification.
@ref Art 11(2), first sentence (src:141)
GIVEN `the case is one referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is possible to inform the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller has informed the data subject accordingly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Duty outcome`
`Art 11(2) the controller informs the data subject that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the case is one referred to in paragraph 1` AND `the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "Where"): "Where, in cases referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject, the controller shall inform the data subject accordingly"
        IF NOT (`it is possible to inform the data subject`)
        THEN JUST `the duty does not arise`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "if"): "the controller shall inform the data subject accordingly, if possible"
        IF `the controller has informed the data subject accordingly`
        THEN JUST `the duty arises and is met`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the duty arises and is not met`
        -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question (split site (i))): "the controller shall inform the data subject accordingly, if possible"

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: no time limit, no consequence (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
@ref Art 11(2), first sentence, regulative form (src:141-141)
GIVEN `the duty arises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Role in the Regulation` `Art 11(2) action`
`Art 11(2) the controller must inform the data subject accordingly` MEANS
    IF `the duty arises`
    THEN PARTY `controller`
         MUST `Art 11(2) inform the data subject accordingly`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

#TRACE `Art 11(2) the controller must inform the data subject accordingly` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `controller` DOES `Art 11(2) inform the data subject accordingly` AT 4
-- Result on the main build: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `Art 11(2) the controller must inform the data subject accordingly` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1000)
-- Result on the main build: the obligation is still standing (no deadline, so no breach).

§ `Article 11(2), second sentence: Articles 15 to 20`

-- src:141 | 2. Where, in cases referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject, the controller shall inform the data subject accordingly, if possible. In such cases, Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject, for the purpose of exercising his or her rights under those articles, provides additional information enabling his or her identification.
@ref Art 11(2), second sentence (src:141)
GIVEN `the case is one referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data subject, for the purpose of exercising his or her rights under Articles 15 to 20, has provided additional information enabling his or her identification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 11(2) Articles 15 to 20 are disapplied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the case is one referred to in paragraph 1` AND `the controller is able to demonstrate that it is not in a position to identify the data subject`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such cases" are the cases of the first sentence; elsewhere Articles 15 to 20 are not spoken of
        IF `the data subject, for the purpose of exercising his or her rights under Articles 15 to 20, has provided additional information enabling his or her identification`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "except where"): "Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply except where the data subject, for the purpose of exercising his or her rights under those articles, provides additional information enabling his or her identification"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        -- "In such cases, Articles 15 to 20 shall not apply"
